Ladybird shrinks a float’s margin box by its negative inline margins,
and a float whose margin box has no width left doesn’t narrow the space
beside it. Blink, WebKit, and Gecko all do the same. In Blink,
CreateExclusionArea() clamps the margin-box width at zero, and
ExclusionSpaceInternal::DerivedGeometry::Add() then skips an exclusion
with no width. In Gecko, nsFloatManager::CalculateRegionFor() clamps
the region to no width, which GetFlowArea() skips as empty. And in
WebKit, a negative width is kept: FloatingObjects::logicalLeftOffset()
moves the line start only past a float edge that’s beyond it.
